Views in Odoo (Complete Basic Explanation)
Odoo mein View ka matlab hai kisi Model ke data ko user interface (screen) par kis tarah display karna hai.
Simple example:
Tumhare paas student.py model hai, jisme Student Name, Email, Phone, Age fields hain.

Ab in fields ko screen par:
- Table mein dikhana hai → List View
- Form mein dikhana hai → Form View
- Cards mein dikhana hai → Kanban View
Ye sab Views ke through hota hai.
1. Important Views in Odoo 18

1. List View (list)
Multiple records ko rows aur columns mein display karta hai.
Example: All Students ki list.
<list>
    <field name="name"/>
    <field name="email"/>
    <field name="age"/>
</list>

2. Form View (form)
Ek record ki complete details display karta hai.
Example: Rahul ki complete student details.
<form>
    <sheet>
        <group>
            <field name="name"/>
            <field name="email"/>
        </group>
    </sheet>
</form>

3. Kanban View (kanban)
Records ko cards ke form mein show karta hai.
Example: Student Profile Cards.
<kanban>
    <templates>
        <t t-name="card">
            <field name="name"/>
        </t>
    </templates>
</kanban>

4. Search View (search)
Records ko search, filter aur group karne ke liye.
<search>
    <field name="name"/>
    <field name="email"/>
</search>

5. Calendar View (calendar)
Records ko calendar format mein display karta hai.
Example: Student Admission Dates.
<calendar date_start="admission">
    <field name="name"/>
</calendar>

6. Pivot View (pivot)
Data analysis aur summary reports ke liye.
Example: Department-wise Fees.
<pivot>
    <field name="department_id" type="row"/>
    <field name="fees" type="measure"/>
</pivot>

7. Graph View (graph)
Data ko graphical format mein show karta hai.

Example: Student Fees Chart.
<graph type="bar">
    <field name="department_id"/>
    <field name="fees" type="measure"/>
</graph>

